@startuml
title Workflow definition lifecycle: draft to pinned run to migration
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECF5FC
  BorderColor #477B9B
  StartColor #2F7C5A
  EndColor #7D478F
  ArrowColor #496174
}

state "Draft" as Draft #DCEEFF
state "Publishable" as Publishable #E9F5EA
state "Deployed" as Deployed #D9EFDF
state "Pinned run" as PinnedRun #FFE0C8

[*] --> Draft : create team
Draft --> Draft : save\n(permissive: diagnostics shown,\nerrors do not block)
Draft --> Publishable : assertPublishable\n[zero error-severity diagnostics]
Publishable --> Draft : edit
Publishable --> Deployed : deploy\n/ insertSigned (version compare-and-set)\npublishes the team contract and manifest
Deployed --> Draft : edit (new draft revision;\ndeployed contract unchanged)
Deployed --> PinnedRun : run prepare/send\n/ pin <latex>H(\mathrm{definition})</latex> in the run register
PinnedRun --> PinnedRun : migrate command\n[from-hash matches pinned hash]\n/ apply statePatch (set / remove),\nrebind team + definition, runMigrated

note right of Deployed #EAF7EE
The registry publication is versioned: insertSigned
rejects a stale version, so deployment is a
compare-and-set on the team URI.
end note
note bottom of PinnedRun #FFF3C9
Every run pins the exact definition hash it was
prepared against. Later edits or deployments never
change a live run; only an authenticated migrate
command with the matching source hash can rebind it.
end note
@enduml
